        [
          "Reach",
          "Wins by a mile: built into every browser and language, and everything around it, from jq to gateways",
          "Needs its own reader everywhere"
        ],
        [
          "Speed",
          "Parsers are heavily optimized",
          "Unknown: only a small prototype reader exists"
        ],
        [
          "Reading with no model",
          "Wins: field names and structure are all there",
          "Structure and names, as long as code isn't positional, but no checking"
        ],
        [
          "Exact values",
          "Strings by convention",
          "Wins: 89.00d, big integers and enums are themselves"
        ],
        [
          "Signing and caching",
          "Equal objects can differ in bytes, so signing needs a separate canonical form, such as the IETF's JSON Canonicalization Scheme (its RFC 8785, not one of Incan's)",
          "Wins: one specified printer, so a signature or strong ETag can cover the exact bytes with no separate canonical form. The canonical hash can't stand in for either, because it leaves out canonical=false fields, and the object hash leaves out trunders, so each covers only that narrower projection"
        ],
        [
          "Schema drift",
          "Nothing in the response says which schema it follows",
          "Wins: ___model_hash says exactly which model wrote it"
        ],
        [
          "Saving the response",
          "Needs a mapping back to types first",
          "Wins: crumble it as it is"
        ]
      ],
